# Binaries.
# `pantheon` is now a SYMLINK to the per-backend binary the last build produced
# (Makefile: PN_BIN / PN_COMPAT_BIN); each backend also writes its own file, so
# a TT build can no longer overwrite a deployed CUDA one. All of them are
# ignored, and the combination names too, so a `make USE_CUDA=1 USE_TT=1` tree
# stays clean.
pantheon
pantheon-cpu
pantheon-cuda
pantheon-tt
pantheon-metal
pantheon-cuda-tt
pantheon-cuda-metal
pantheon-tt-metal
pantheon-cuda-tt-metal
tests/test_backend_guard
tests/test_build
tests/test_graph_capture_concurrency
tests/test_attn_ring_retry
tests/test_graph_capture_retry
tests/test_gguf
tests/test_arena
tests/test_qmv
tests/test_simd
tests/test_chat
tests/test_chat_request
tests/test_tool_calling
